The '''''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle''', also known as the '''''Zeta''-class cargo shuttle''' or the '''''Zeta''-class Imperial shuttle''', or simply the '''Zeta-class shuttle''' was a type of [[cargo shuttle]] used by the [[Galactic Empire]] in its fight against the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. They were instrumental in carrying [[kyber crystal]]s during the construction of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:Zeta-class_interior.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Interior cockpit of the ''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle.]]
The ''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo [[Shuttle]] featured two levels: an upper deck that housed the ship's controls, and a ventral cargo deck that could be detached and dropped off at a location. The [[shuttle]] also had four wings that retracted inwards when landing and outwards when in flight, similar to the [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

It was of similar appearance to the [[Eta-class supply barge|''Eta''-class supply barge]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> The shuttle's ventral cargo pod used standardized umbilicals and docking sleeves for grabbing onto docking clamps. These pods drew power from the Zeta's reactor plant, which also provided energy for specific cargo such as refrigeration or life support.<ref name="CV">''[[Star Wars Complete Vehicles, New Edition]]''</ref>

In terms of armament, the shuttles featured two wing-mounted [[KV22 heavy laser cannon]]s and three hull-mounted [[Taim & Bak]] [[KX7 laser cannon]]s. Skilled pilots did not need to fully land the shuttles in order to drop off or pick up cargo.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

==History==
===Dawn of rebellion===
[[File:Imperial-Cargo-Shuttle-SWCT.png|thumb|left|250px|A ''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle, with its wings set in flight mode.]]
''Zeta''-class shuttles were used by the Imperial civilian government<ref name="Visual Guide" /> and also during military operations. During the [[Partisans]]'s attack on a Galactic Empire refinery in [[Kashyyyk]], the [[Padawan]] [[Jedi]] [[Cal Kestis]], who had stolen an [[All Terrain Armored Transport|AT-AT]] during the confrontation, helped [[Saw Gerrera]] and his allies to move forward and destroyed a ''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle with the [[walker]]. The AT-AT ended up being destroyed along with the shuttle when it was hit by it when it crashed.<ref name="Fallen Order">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order]]''</ref>

In [[9 BBY]], a ''Zeta''-class shuttle was present on the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid-Rim]] [[farming]] planet [[Mapuzo]] when the [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and a young [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] fled to the planet following the [[Search for Princess Leia]] on [[Daiyu]]<ref>{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref>. In the same year, a ''Zeta''-class shuttle landed in the [[Narkis Highlands]] outside [[The Archive]] on [[Jedha]] during the Imperial [[Raid on the Archive]].<ref>''[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]''</ref>

In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="AndorDate">{{AndorDate|112}}</ref> a ''Zeta''-class shuttle was landed on the newly [[Ferrix occupation|Imperial occupied]]-planet [[Ferrix]] as [[ISB Supervisor]] [[Dedra Meero]] arrived on world aboard a [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]].<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref> In [[2 BBY]],<ref name="2BBYDate">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]'' establishes that the [[escape from the Senate]] occurred between the [[Ghorman Massacre]] and before [[Operation Handoff]], both of which occur in [[2 BBY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> a ''Zeta''-class shuttle was parked at the [[Imperial Senate]] loading dock prior to [[Mon Mothma]]'s denouncement of the [[Ghorman Massacre|Ghorman massacre]] and her [[Escape from the Senate|subsequent evacuation]] from [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Welcome">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref>

===War with rebels===
{{Quote|Well done. You're a rebel now.|K-2SO to Bodhi Rook, after the latter turned ''SW-0608''{{'s}} weapons on a squad of stormtroopers|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:ZetaClassShuttle-CGSWG.png|thumb|right|300px|A ''Zeta''-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle]]
During the mining of [[Jedha]], many of these shuttles were used during the Imperial occupation of Jedha to transport [[kyber crystal]]s for the purpose of powering the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star's]] [[superlaser]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> Before the [[Jedha insurgency]] started, the [[Guardians of the Whills]] [[Baze Malbus]] and [[Chirrut Îmwe]] raided an Imperial supply convoy dropped off at [[LZ-Cresh]] by a [[Unidentified Zeta-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle|cargo shuttle]].<ref name="Guardians">[[Guardians of the Whills (novel)|''Guardians of the Whills'']]</ref> As the Jedha insurgency began with the arrival of the Partisans, the ''Zeta''-class continued to see use on Jedha until the Imperial withdrawal. At least five shuttles were stationed at the [[Eadu Flight Station]] at the time of the [[Mission to Eadu]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> in [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> One of these shuttles, [[SW-0608]], would be stolen by [[Rogue One]]. A number of these shuttles were also present for the [[Battle of Scarif]], a successful attempt by the Rebel Alliance to steal the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the Death Star.<ref name="Rogue One" />

At least five were present at the [[Fondor Shipyards]] when they were [[Attack on Fondor|attacked]] by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]].<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> Numerous Zeta-class shuttles could be found at the [[Remitik system munitions depot]]. Two shuttles carrying the explosive compound [[baradium]] were stolen by [[Titan Squadron]] as a [[Battle in the Remitik system|skirmish]] with [[New Republic]] forces occurred.<ref name="Squadrons" />

